---
layout: layout.njk
title: Health Check assessment
seo_title: "Production Finance Health Check assessment | Tubes"
description: "Tell us how the six areas of your production finance process stand today, so we can prepare for your Health Check session."
permalink: /production-finance-health-check/assessment/
noindex: true
---
{#- De vragenlijst van de Health Check, op een eigen adres zodat de link ook
    los verstuurd kan worden aan iemand die al een sessie heeft staan.

    Opzet: drie stappen van twee vragen. Elke stap is een thema, en de kolom
    rechts legt dat thema uit. Twee vragen per scherm in plaats van zes op
    een rij: zo krijgt elke vraag de aandacht die hij verdient.

    Binnenkomen kan op twee manieren:
      ?ref=<id>  vanaf het bedankscherm; dan weten we al wie het is en hoeft
                 het e-mailadres niet gevraagd te worden.
      kaal       dan vragen we het zakelijke e-mailadres om de antwoorden aan
                 de aanvraag te kunnen koppelen.

    Bewust noindex: een vragenlijst voor genodigden, geen marketingpagina. -#}

{%- set assessOptions = [
  { value: "Strong", tone: "good" },
  { value: "Could improve", tone: "mid" },
  { value: "Opportunity", tone: "low" }
] -%}

{%- set steps = [
  {
    num: 1,
    theme: "Planning and budgeting",
    heading: "How the budget is built, and what happens once it is approved",
    areas: [
      {
        key: "budget_structure",
        short: "budget structure",
        label: "Budget structure and version control",
        hint: "How budgets are built and changed, and how you know which version counts."
      },
      {
        key: "budget_handover",
        short: "the handover to production",
        label: "Budget to production handover",
        hint: "What happens after approval, and how the people spending the money get a working budget."
      }
    ],
    friction: "Most budgets survive approval intact. What tends to break is everything after it: a version sitting in someone's inbox, a working budget rebuilt by hand, and two numbers that no longer agree.",
    reading: [
      { label: "How to Build a Production Budget", url: "/insights/how-to-build-a-production-budget/" },
      { label: "Above the Line vs Below the Line", url: "/insights/above-the-line-vs-below-the-line/" }
    ]
  },
  {
    num: 2,
    theme: "Spending and control",
    heading: "What actually gets spent, and who is allowed to commit it",
    areas: [
      {
        key: "actuals",
        short: "actuals",
        label: "Actuals and reconciliation",
        hint: "How real costs come in, how they are coded, and how they get matched back to the budget."
      },
      {
        key: "approvals",
        short: "approvals",
        label: "Approvals and controls",
        hint: "Who may commit spend, who may change a budget, and how that is recorded."
      }
    ],
    friction: "Costs rarely arrive in the shape the budget expects. The work of making them line up is usually invisible, usually manual, and usually done by one person under time pressure.",
    reading: [
      { label: "How Much Contingency Does a Production Need?", url: "/insights/how-much-contingency-does-a-production-need/" }
    ]
  },
  {
    num: 3,
    theme: "Forecasting and reporting",
    heading: "Knowing where this will land, and who gets told in time",
    areas: [
      {
        key: "forecasting",
        short: "forecasting",
        label: "Forecasting",
        hint: "How commitments, costs to date and remaining costs add up to an expected final cost."
      },
      {
        key: "reporting",
        short: "reporting",
        label: "Reporting and visibility",
        hint: "Who gets reliable financial information, in what form, and how long it takes to produce."
      }
    ],
    friction: "A report that takes three days to build is a report about last week. The question is not only whether the numbers are right, but whether they arrive while you can still do something about them.",
    reading: [
      { label: "What Is a Production Cost Report?", url: "/insights/what-is-a-production-cost-report/" }
    ]
  }
] -%}

<section class="section section-hero theme-light hc-assess-page">
  <div class="container hc-assess-grid">

    <div class="hc-assess-main">
      <span class="kicker">Production Finance Health Check</span>
      <h1>How does your process stand today?</h1>
      <p class="hc-lead">Six questions in three short steps. Your own impression is all we need. We go through each area properly during the session, so there are no wrong answers here.</p>

      <form class="hc-form hc-assess-form" id="hc-assessment" data-hc-assess-form novalidate>
        <input type="text" name="company_website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" style="display:none" data-1p-ignore data-lpignore="true" data-form-type="other">

        <div class="hc-form-card">
          <div class="hc-progress" data-hc-progress>
            {%- for step in steps %}
            <span class="hc-progress-bar{% if loop.first %} is-current{% endif %}" data-hc-progress-bar="{{ step.num }}">
              <span class="visually-hidden">Step {{ step.num }}: {{ step.theme }}</span>
            </span>
            {%- endfor %}
            <span class="hc-progress-bar" data-hc-progress-bar="4"><span class="visually-hidden">Step 4: your summary</span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="hc-assess-identify" data-hc-identify>
            <label class="hc-field" for="hc-assessment-email">Business email address
              <input type="email" id="hc-assessment-email" name="email" inputmode="email" autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" required>
            </label>
            <p class="hc-help">So we can match your answers to your Health Check request.</p>
          </div>

          {%- for step in steps %}
          <div class="hc-stage" data-hc-stage="{{ step.num }}"{% if not loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>
            <p class="hc-stage-meta"><span class="hc-step-count">Step {{ step.num }} of 4</span> {{ step.theme }}</p>
            <h2 class="hc-stage-heading">{{ step.heading }}</h2>

            {%- for area in step.areas %}
            <fieldset class="hc-question" data-short="{{ area.short }}">
              <legend class="hc-question-label">{{ area.label }}</legend>
              <p class="hc-question-hint">{{ area.hint }}</p>
              <div class="hc-assess-options">
                {%- for option in assessOptions %}
                <label class="hc-opt hc-opt-{{ option.tone }}">
                  <input type="radio" name="{{ area.key }}" value="{{ option.value }}">
                  <span>{{ option.value }}</span>
                </label>
                {%- endfor %}
              </div>
            </fieldset>
            {%- endfor %}

            {%- if loop.last %}
            <label class="hc-field hc-assess-notes" for="hc-assessment-notes">Anything you would like us to look at? <span class="hc-optional">(optional)</span>
              <textarea id="hc-assessment-notes" name="notes" rows="4" placeholder="A recurring problem, a production that went sideways, a report nobody trusts."></textarea>
            </label>
            {%- endif %}

            <div class="hc-stage-actions">
              {%- if loop.last %}
              <button type="submit" class="button button-primary hc-submit">See my summary</button>
              {%- else %}
              <button type="button" class="button button-primary hc-next" data-hc-next="{{ step.num + 1 }}">Continue</button>
              {%- endif %}
              {%- if not loop.first %}
              <button type="button" class="hc-back" data-hc-back="{{ step.num - 1 }}">Back</button>
              {%- endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
          {%- endfor %}

          <p class="form-status hc-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

          {#- Stap 4 is de uitkomst: hun eigen antwoorden op een rij, plus waar
              we mee beginnen. Geen cijfer en geen oordeel; dat zou een uitslag
              suggereren die pas uit het gesprek kan komen. -#}
          <div class="hc-stage hc-result" data-hc-stage="4" hidden>
            <p class="hc-stage-meta"><span class="hc-step-count">Step 4 of 4</span> Your summary</p>
            <h2 class="hc-stage-heading">This is what you told us</h2>
            <p class="hc-result-intro">Received, thank you. Nothing is scored here: this is your own reading of the six areas, and it sets the agenda for the session.</p>

            <ol class="hc-result-list" data-hc-result-list></ol>

            <div class="hc-result-focus" data-hc-result-focus></div>

            <p class="hc-done-note">Nothing else to do for now. If you have not heard from us yet, we will be in touch shortly to arrange a time.</p>
          </div>

          <p class="hc-privacy">We use your answers only to prepare your Health Check. We do not add you to a mailing list and we do not pass your details on. See how we handle data in <a href="/compliance/">security and compliance</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    {#- Rechts loopt mee met de stap: wat dit thema inhoudt, waar het meestal
        misgaat, en iets om te lezen terwijl je nadenkt. -#}
    <aside class="hc-assess-aside">
      {%- for step in steps %}
      <div class="hc-theme" data-hc-theme="{{ step.num }}"{% if not loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>
        <span class="hc-theme-kicker">Step {{ step.num }} of 4</span>
        <h2 class="hc-theme-title">{{ step.theme }}</h2>

        <p class="hc-theme-friction">{{ step.friction }}</p>

        <div class="hc-theme-reading">
          <p class="hc-theme-reading-title">While you think it over</p>
          <ul>
            {%- for item in step.reading %}
            <li><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.label }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}

      <div class="hc-theme" data-hc-theme="4" hidden>
        <span class="hc-theme-kicker">Step 4 of 4</span>
        <h2 class="hc-theme-title">What happens next</h2>
        <ol class="hc-next-list">
          <li>We read your answers before we speak, so we do not spend the session on the basics.</li>
          <li>45 minutes together, going through each area properly.</li>
          <li>A short written summary: the three main opportunities, where the manual work sits, and what to improve first.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="hc-scan-note">If Tubes can solve one of the things we find, we will show you that part. There is no obligation to continue.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="hc-theme-key">
        <p class="hc-scan-key">The three labels</p>
        <ul class="hc-label-list">
          <li><span class="chip chip-mint">Strong</span><span>This works. Nobody loses time over it and you trust the numbers.</span></li>
          <li><span class="chip chip-amber">Could improve</span><span>Workable, but it costs time, or it only works because one person knows how.</span></li>
          <li><span class="chip chip-lavender">Opportunity</span><span>This is where things go wrong, get lost, or arrive too late to act on.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="hc-scan-note">No score out of ten. Your answers set the agenda for the session, they are not the verdict.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>
</section>
